    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a lineup anchored by the high-floor efficiency of **Junior Caminero** (67.98) and the elite speed-centric upside of **Trea Turner** (76.82). **Trea Turner** draws a highly favorable matchup against Abbott, where the combination of leadoff positioning and a positive platoon edge provides our highest score of the day. Meanwhile, **Carson Benge** (63.27) and **Casey Schmitt** (63.20) are strong starts; **Carson Benge** benefits immensely from a high-upside matchup against Littell, while **Casey Schmitt**\u2019s score is bolstered by a favorable SP delivery profile that significantly increases his stolen base equity\u2014a critical consideration given our strategic emphasis on the scarcest category, SB.\n\nThe decision to bench **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (45.46) was the tightest call on the roster. While **Pete Crow-Armstrong** provides excellent speed, his projected efficiency was suppressed by a difficult platoon matchup against Harrison and a bottom-of-the-order assignment that limits his run-production potential. Consequently, he falls below the threshold for immediate starting consideration behind the balanced production of **Hyeseong Kim** (57.43), whose elite SP skill factor keeps him in the lineup despite a lower-order placement. \n\nWe are monitoring risk factors across the board, specifically for **Dillon Dingler** (46.13) and **Kazuma Okamoto** (47.77), both of whom are hovering near the floor due to difficult matchups against Bibee and Schlittler, respectively. **Dillon Dingler** faces a significant platoon penalty today, and **Kazuma Okamoto** is contending with a strong SP skill metric from his opponent. Should lineup adjustments surface for our reserves, we remain ready to pivot, though with **Zac Veen** currently stationed in the minors and **Caleb Durbin** absent from the confirmed starting lineup, our depth is currently constrained to the active starters.",
